{#
Purpose: Translate a value through a mapping dict, returning the mapped value if
present, or the original value otherwise. Used to bridge Data-Model vs
base-collection value spellings (e.g. 'none' -> 'no', true -> 'false', etc).

Usage: {{ translate(value, {'src1': 'dst1', 'src2': 'dst2'}) }}

Note: Callers pre-resolve missing fields via `default(defaults.<profile>.<field>)`
and hand the resolved value in. The macro is pure — it never reaches into
`defaults` on its own, because only the caller knows which profile applies.
#}
{% macro translate(value, mapping) -%}
{%- if value in mapping -%}{{ mapping[value] }}{%- else -%}{{ value }}{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
